course: dictionary
lesson: 11498
title: Agitated: worried or stirred up
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Agitated is an adjective. It describes how someone feels or how something moves. When a person is agitated, they are worried, nervous and upset, and they cannot keep calm. «The hen was agitated when the fox came near the fence.» The hen is not just scared for a moment. The word shows she is upset and cannot settle.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Mum got agitated about the late train.» She paces up and down, checks her watch and talks fast. These actions show that agitated means restless and worried, not happy or relaxed.
explain: Agitated can also describe a liquid that is shaken or stirred. «Shake the bottle hard and the juice becomes agitated.» Here the word means the liquid is moving about, not that anyone is upset. Always ask what the sentence is about: a person or a liquid? That tells you which meaning to use.
fact: Agitated means worried, nervous and upset, and unable to keep calm.
fact: Agitated can also mean shaken or stirred, as a liquid.
fact: Agitated is the past form of the verb «agitate», so you may see both words in stories and science texts.
fact: Clues like pacing, fidgeting and talking fast show that a character is agitated.
fact: «Calm» is the opposite of agitated, so a calm person is not agitated.
exercise: «Ravi kept pacing the room and fidgeting, because he was agitated about his test.» What does agitated mean? | Fast asleep | Very tall | *Worried and unable to keep calm | Happy and relaxed
exercise: «Shake the bottle of juice hard and the liquid becomes agitated.» What does agitated mean here? | Frozen solid | Painted bright red | Cold to touch | *Shaken or stirred
exercise: «The old dog grew agitated when the thunder began.» Find and copy the word that means worried and upset. | thunder | old | *agitated | dog
test: «Mia was agitated before her swimming race, so she tapped her feet and kept looking at the clock.» What does agitated mean? | Happy and full of cake | Very wet | Calm and sleepy | *Nervous and unable to keep calm
test: Dad says agitated is the opposite of calm. Is he right? | Yes, it means very quiet | No, agitated means very happy | *Yes, agitated means unable to keep calm | No, it means very old
exam: «The sea grew agitated in the storm, with huge waves crashing about.» What does agitated mean here? | Sweet to taste | Frozen solid | Perfectly still | *Rough and stirred up
